OL,3,GNEWSADozens help singing shopworker
OL,4,Arecover from setback
OL,5,
OL,6,FDozens of people have gathered outside
OL,7,Fa convenience store in Nottingham to
OL,8,Fsupport their favourite singing staff
OL,9,Fmember.
OL,11,FMiles Green, who has Down's Syndrome,
OL,12,Fcan often be found singing on the
OL,13,Fcorner of Gedling Road, in Carlton,
OL,14,Fafter his shift at the nearby One Stop
OL,15,Fshop, as passers-by beep their car
OL,16,Fhorns in support.
OL,18,FBut his confidence was knocked after
OL,19,Fpolice were called last week over
OL,20,Fconcerns for the 28-year-old's welfare,
OL,21,Fleaving him fearing he would no longer
OL,22,Fbe able to sing.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
